that license when redistributing the compiled device kernels.


The PyTorch checkpoint adapter uses a vendored pytorch-reader 0.22.0 copy under
vendor/pytorch-reader, derived from tracel-ai/burn at
b8d75ad07f426537594a5beb9309d62d916bcf05 under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The complete
upstream license texts, original file hashes, modification list and attribution
notice are retained in that directory (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE, NOTICE,
provenance.json). The vendored source is the frozen V3 prototype unchanged;
only Cargo.toml is adapted for the Oxide path build. Deflated ZIP remains
unsupported by the prototype verifier, and Oxide rejects compressed entries for
backend publication rather than accepting its quadratic range access.
